    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm prepping for a meeting with a new raw material supplier next week. We're looking to set up a master service agreement (MSA) for long-term supply. Can you give me a checklist of standard terms and conditions I should make sure are in there? Specifically, I'm worried about protecting us against sudden price hikes and supply chain volatility. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, preparing for a meeting with a raw material supplier is crucial. Your checklist for the MSA should include terms like:\n\n- Price adjustment clauses that outline conditions under which prices may change, and potential caps on value changes.\n- Volume commitment reviews to ensure the supplier can meet your demand without incurring large costs or disruptions.\n- Lead time and delivery schedule commitments, to ensure you have sufficient notice and time to plan for any changes or disruptions.\n- Quality and specification terms to define the material standards and performance you expect.\n- Penalty clauses for late deliveries or failure to meet agreed-upon standards.\n- A force majeure clause to outline what would be considered unforeseeable events that could relieve both parties from their obligations.",
      "source": "target",
