      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i also want to add some language regarding \"bad faith\" or deceptive practices, where they might intentionally withhold supply to force a price renegotiation. what kind of specific wording or audit rights can we include to catch them if they're being dishonest about their capacity or costs?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address concerns involving \"bad faith or deceptive practices,\" your force majeure clause can include:\n\n- **Intention to Harm Clause:** Define as force majeure an act done with an intention to harm you by limiting the supplier's ability to fulfil obligations.\n\n- **Right to Audit:** Include a right to inspect the supplier's operations, financial records, and inventory levels at reasonable times under normal business hours, during which you can verify their claims regarding capacity or costs.\n\n- **Good Faith Requirement:** Mandate that both parties must act in good faith and with fair dealing in providing and verifying information about their operations.\n\n- **Consequences for Bad Faith:** Clearly state the repercussions for the supplier in case of proof of bad faith, like termination of the agreement, compensation for costs incurred, and covering legal fees.",
